/*
 * EXAMPLE 11 — MinHeap<Integer>, singular case.
 *
 * 9 is inserted first, then 4, then 7.  The order matters: the smallest value
 * arrives SECOND, so it has to sift up past a value already in the heap, and the
 * third insertion then has to leave it alone.  A heap that only ever appended
 * would answer 9 to peekMin and fail on the spot.
 *
 * Neither peekMin nor extractMin binds anything here — they take no parameters,
 * and the value each returns is the heap's answer, not the caller's.
 */
test MinHeapDryRun {
    sequence: insert -> insert -> insert -> peekMin -> extractMin;

    inputs {
        insert[0].value = 9;
        insert[1].value = 4;
        insert[2].value = 7;
    }
}
